WEBVTT

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.830
I guess we'll have to send out our docking
clearance signal pretty soon, huh?

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.450
Stop your bitching and just hold on a minute.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:22.790
I'm tellin' you to leave this to me!

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.870
You really want me to leave it all to you?

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:30.090
It ain't exactly easy to believe the words of a guy
who's still flipping through the manual at this point.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.510
Sending a signal is one of the most
fundamental things for a sailor!

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.850
You really forgot how to do it, didn't you?

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.060
Would you shut the hell up?!

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.440
I don't see how I'm going to learn anything with
you running your damn mouth off like that!

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.270
So then, you did forget.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:51.030
I am reviewing how to do it! Reviewing!
Don't count me in with senile old fools like you!

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.990
Hah! Take a good look ahead of us.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.030
You can't afford to be taking your
time "reviewing" things.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:55.950
Huh?

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.740
Damn! This sucks!

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.990
Uh, lessee...

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.910
Relax!
Uh, lessee...

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:06.620
You think I can just sit back and relax?!
Um, lessee... Okay...

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.180
Hey, I wonder if Bishop and Swamp
are doing all right?

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.100
Well, probably not.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.600
You got it!

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.560
There's no way those two are doing all right.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.940
They'll probably be at each other's
throats any minute now.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.770
I can tell you that they're definitely
at each other's throats already!

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.280
No doubt!

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.660
Then why did you put those two together?

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.030
'Cuz that oughta make things more entertaining!

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:40.950
Huh?

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.950
Yeah, yeah! Entertaining!

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:43.950
HUH?

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.950
Oh, damn!

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.460
We should have wired up a camera somewhere!

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.840
A hidden camera!

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.750
Nah, no way!

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:56.300
I mean, that would be like watching a mystery movie
where you already know what happens!

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.390
Yeah, I guess so. You're absolutely right.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.200
Hokorimamire no bonnet

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.620
yubi de kyou o kizamu

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.080
Toori ame ga sugiru koro

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.920
ai no you ni kieta

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:37.170
Kokoro no naka nakusenu mono aru kara

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:43.300
Mienai tsubasa habatakase

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:50.520
Koredemo katto fuku kaze ni mukaiuchi

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:57.780
Yuruginai kimochi de tachimukatteku no sa, go!

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:04.700
Sunabokori mau yakusoku no basho e

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:10.670
Oretachi wa hashiritsuzukete yuku

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.840
Konya koso

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.340
Koete yaru

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:25.100
Ano saki made

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:37.860
Episode 9       Jupiter

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.910
That monster appetite of yours
hasn't changed any, has it?

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.750
Ah, morning.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.370
You're up early, aren't you?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.250
Not as early as you.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:04:00.300
Angelica... Please... wait up...

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.430
Hey, tell me something.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.760
Do your sisters all get up as early as you?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.180
What difference does it make?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.140
Not like it does make any difference to me.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.110
Only twenty-four hours until the bomb drops...

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.820
Hopefully, we'll be able to see
another sunrise like this.

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.540
Oh, we'll see it all right.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.750
Well, you're sure confident.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.620
So what are you going to do now?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.960
Wait.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:35.790
Wait?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:39.170
Right, all we have to do is wait for Mister.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.090
As long as Mister is after the
same thing your mother is,

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.220
he will come here without fail.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:53.100
With you, it's always "Mister this" and "Mister that."

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.400
Huh? Have you already eaten breakfast?!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.320
You're always eating. I'm amazed
you don't get sick of it!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.120
As they say, "You can't wait for Mister
on an empty stomach."

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.870
The proverb is "You can't wage war
on an empty stomach."

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.630
These are orders from Headquarters!

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.710
Yes, so I see.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.670
Could you please sign for it?

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.550
Here, right?

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.640
You've come quite a long way. Good work.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:35.230
If... If you wouldn't mind,
could you please refuel our ship?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.690
We were also hoping to have a mechanic
take a look at our left engine,

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:41.400
since it doesn't seem to be doing too well.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.570
Understood. I'll make the necessary arrangements.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.780
Please wait over there until we're finished.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.360
Yes, sir. Thank you very much.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.620
Thank you!
Yes, sir. Thank you very much.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.500
Whew!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:00.500
Cripes, you can't send a signal and you can barely
hold it together when it's time to act.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.170
You wouldn't be able to do a
damn thing without me.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:06.840
You can't blame me!
There's a whole planet on the line here!

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.260
When it does come down to it, I...

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.930
Hey, where are you going?!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.180
We're not gonna get anywhere
just sitting around here.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.350
Whoa! Wait a minute!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.020
H..Hey!

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.610
Yep...

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.030
That's the photonic bomb.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.490
This thing, huh?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:32.410
How are we gonna get up close and personal
with that big-ass thing from here?

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:36.040
If it were just a little closer to the ship,
we'd be able to slip in somehow.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.790
So naive as you are,
you still sense danger, do you?

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.500
Shut the hell up!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.500
Don't you have any ideas?

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:46.420
Well, now, if it were me...

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.930
You've got no idea, do you?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.100
Don't interrupt me while I'm thinking!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.930
Look who's talking!

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.220
What was that?!

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.390
Hey, who was it that got that
signal sent out for you?

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:02.020
Oh yeah, thank you so much, sir!

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.570
You lookin' for a fight?! You little...

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.320
What's that ship?

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.160
Hell if I know!

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.720
That's Malcolm!

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.340
Pardon me.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:38.270
Well, let's get started.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.560
The important thing now is how
we are going to end this war.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.820
I'm sure you'll agree, Representative Boniek.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:53.160
The Graceland Liberation Forces will
have to show understanding,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.950
seeing as how the Secretary of Foreign Affairs
has come in person, no?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.370
Thank you.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:01.870
After all, we certainly don't want to
leave behind a sullied legacy

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.500
as politicians who obliterated a planet.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:08.130
Then don't resort to dropping the photonic bomb.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.130
Damn! What the heck are they doing in there?

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.510
You're the ones who have driven us to it!

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:18.140
You're sitting here today because
you've taken things so far!

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.060
Forgive me.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:26.690
We almost ended up going around
in circles again, as always.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.190
April, aren't we there yet?!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:35.370
I'm bored too! I can't take it anymore!

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.030
Come on, I wanna play now!

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:37.330
I wanna play too!
Come on, I wanna play now!

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:39.240
I wanna play too!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.290
Hold on just a little longer.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:45.580
I'll let you romp around to your hearts'
content when we get there.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.300
<i>No sleeping, Dece!</i>

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.970
<i>Okay...</i>

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.510
God dammit!

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.470
What are we supposed to do?!

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.610
I see, that'll work.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.730
I'm gonna go get me one.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.330
Hi there.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.830
Idiot! What the hell do you think you're doing?!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.710
Just watch.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.920
H..Hey!

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.960
Pardon me!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.050
I've brought you gentlemen some orange juice.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.970
We haven't asked for any such thing!

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:46.690
But I was told just a few minutes ago,
so I brought it all over here as quick as I could.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.400
There's some pineapple juice too, and...

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:48.770
All right already!
There's some pineapple juice too, and...

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.150
All right already!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:53.110
Fine, just leave it over there and get out!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.650
Yes, sir...

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.160
I'll do just that then.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.570
Pardon the intrusion!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.910
What are you doing going off
on your own like that?!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.120
I thought I told you.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.790
When it comes down to it, I can perform.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:13.250
All right, gentlemen, we're just about out of time,
so let's continue with the proceedings.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.480
Perfect!

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.230
Except it is pretty cramped in here.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.310
Shut up!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.940
Just keep it down and listen!

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.480
Why did you chose a place like this?!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.860
We're least likely to get caught here.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.820
Leave it to an old geezer to think up
something like this!

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:41.450
Don't treat me like an old geezer.
I did send the signal, right?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.790
You're still harping on that? Man, I can't take it!

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:45.830
Achoo!

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.580
Shut up! Someone's going to hear us!

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:51.500
Just do something about that damn hair...

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:52.790
ACHOO!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.300
Hey, Mister.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.720
Is it okay to head directly towards
Gigabanks like this?

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:08.560
It's not okay.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.600
Yeah, of course not.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.980
Franca...

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:16.780
Do you know why it's not okay to
head straight for Gigabanks?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:22.370
Because we might get ambushed by Marciano.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.370
Right?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.030
That is correct!

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.790
They should have an ambush set up.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.170
But seeing as how we're up against a time limit,

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:34.880
we have to roll with the punches,
whatever they might be.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.210
And well, if it were me,

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:39.340
I'd line my people up before we got to Graceland.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:41.220
Huh?

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.090
Picking up something on radar.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.640
You see?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.720
I wouldn't say being right about that
is something to be glad about!

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.430
How many, all told?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.400
It looks like about a dozen.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:56.440
We sure are popular!

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:00.240
I'm more into more chic women who
have a sense of class though.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.410
All hail Queen Angelica!

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.830
Katana, please!

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.160
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.670
There's a whole bunch of them coming for us,
so playing around is only going to get us killed.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:13.830
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.340
All right, you two.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:16.340
Huh?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.840
Shall we go party with them then?

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:38.070
The Federation's conditions for
peace are as follows...

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.740
One: Upon conclusion of the peace process,

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:45.450
Federal intervention is to be respected with regard
to the drafting of constitutional reform bills.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:49.870
Two: All military weaponry and relevant
development materials,

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:53.920
in addition to all other items that could
potentially be misappropriated,

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.040
will be put under control of the Federation.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.710
Three...

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.180
Hey. Katana!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.970
Set your sights on Graceland!

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.680
There's no need to take out the enemy.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.310
Find an opening and blast on through!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:15.060
You got it!

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.440
Katana, three ships closing from below right!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.400
Roger!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.160
Okay, Octo, Nove and Dece, wake up.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.630
Our objective is the destruction
of the photonic bomb.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:39.500
It's in the Jupiter, the central ship.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.050
Whatever you do, avoid hitting the bomb itself.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.970
From this distance, we'll also be
blown to bits if it explodes.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.050
Is that understood?

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.470
Yes!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:57.310
This will allow Mother to seek out
the "treasure" at her leisure.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:08.410
This peace proposal is very much
in your favor, isn't it?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.160
As these are negotiations,

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.040
we will of course listen to any concerns
that the Liberation Forces might have

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:14.580
<i>as</i> we all feel our way forward.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:19.130
I have serious doubts as to whether you really
intend for us to all feel our way forward.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:26.840
What?

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.140
Marciano's Twelve Sisters?

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.220
Prepare for combat immediately.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.970
Don't let them get near the Jupiter!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:36.350
We did it!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.740
Woo! Woo! Woo! Woo!

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:20.730
We can't afford for anything to happen now,

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.980
so we'll need you to evacuate
this ship and take refuge.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.020
I must ask you to go immediately...

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.990
Let them do as they like.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.110
What?

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:34.450
I don't see why the Guild would have any
need to go after the photonic bomb.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:36.870
Have you made a deal with them?

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.250
Never.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.750
Of course not.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.580
In any case, we need to hurry!

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:45.710
If the photonic bomb detonates here,
then we'll go with it!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.880
It won't be detonating.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.840
However, it is Marciano's Twelve Sisters
we are up against.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:54.430
We will engage them with our full force, but...

00:15:54.430 --> 00:16:00.770
I am telling you that even if the Jupiter is destroyed,
there will be no explosion, Malcolm.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:09.490
There's no photonic bomb housed inside that ship.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.910
There's nothing in it. It's just a fake.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.910
So you've deceived us then?!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.250
Oh, we have not deceived you at all.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:28.920
How could we ever blow up an entire planet by
dropping a single bomb on it from outer space?

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:35.890
I've never heard of such a thing ever
being experimented with or done.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:40.890
But if the bomb is planted deep within the
planet itself, well, that's a different story.

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.900
It can't be!

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:50.320
The real photonic bomb has already been buried
deep beneath the surface of Graceland.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.320
No way!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.530
For real?!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.160
Damn, they're persistent.

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:16.890
The photonic bomb's timer has already been set
and it will explode right on schedule.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:20.220
You see? We haven't deceived you at all.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.390
You are scum.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.940
To stop the photonic bomb that has
been buried underground,

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:29.860
one must either disable the ignition
device directly, or...

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:36.450
enter a code into this remote control
device to halt the countdown.

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:43.660
There are 19 hours, 18 minutes
and 36 seconds remaining.

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:50.420
Okay then, we're running out of time,
so let's wrap up these negotiations.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:51.880
Do we just bust in there?

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:56.260
No, wait. If they come to an agreement,
then everything's still all right.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:58.140
One, two...

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:14.860
we.
re Sorry'

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.110
Oh, damn!

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:27.210
Huh?

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.010
It's...

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:36.800
What is going on here?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:44.810
I trust we can we now say we have met
each other's conditions?

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.060
Then, your signature, please.

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:54.360
Where did you bury the bomb?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:59.320
You can at least tell us that much now.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:02.490
We can't contact our comrades
even if you do tell us.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:07.580
And even if we tried to, I'm sure you've
set up jamming signals.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:12.090
And if we break off negotiations now,
you could hold us in custody.

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:15.000
You've got quite an imagination.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.220
Where did you bury it, during wartime like this?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.220
Godwing...

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.430
The place where the gods descend.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.110
That's right by Gigabanks!

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.200
What did you say?!

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.320
Who are you?!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:45.450
Richard?!

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.000
You traitor!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.750
Let's go!

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.630
We've gotta snatch that remote control device!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:57.210
Right!

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:01.010
There was never any photonic bomb.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.850
You... You fool...

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.350
The Graceland Liberation Forces
will stand firm and fight!

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:36.090
There was someone who once said that at the
very end it's always one's allies who interfere.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.250
I don't believe this!

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:42.300
If they had just let things go,
Graceland would have been all right.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.300
Let's go. This ship is done for!

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.220
They're all complete idiots!

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.940
That's why they get into wars.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.900
May, this is all we'll be needing from you.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:08.490
The bomb is going to be dropped on
this planet in just over half a day.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.700
We might die here.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:15.500
I can't let you get wrapped up in this.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.920
Of course, I'll try to avoid dying too.

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:21.420
After all, I haven't even been
married yet or anything.

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:22.340
And I still haven't...

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:25.550
You still haven't captured Mister either.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.970
Let's part ways here.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:32.270
I've enjoyed all the discussions
we've been able to have.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.480
Thank you.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:38.150
When I tell Mother about you,
she may come to capture you.

00:21:38.150 --> 00:21:40.150
No, she won't!

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:42.030
Why don't you think so?

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:44.450
Because she won't.

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:54.660
May!

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.170
The jamming signals are going full blast.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:01.210
There's no way for us to contact
the Coyote like this.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:04.170
We'll just have to go down there.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.890
How much time left before the bomb goes off?

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:10.510
As much time as we've got left to live, maybe.

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:13.020
Are you still gonna go?

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:14.480
With pleasure!

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:16.730
So do we stop the bomb first...

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:19.860
Or take back Bruce's legacy first?

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:43.170
<i>Hoho o tsutawaru</i>

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:53.180
<i>shizuku doko kara kuru no</i>

00:22:54.020 --> 00:22:58.190
<i>Oshiete...</i>

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:04.480
<i>Makimodosenai</i>

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:11.030
<i>jikan to iu ruuru ni</i>

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:19.250
<i>munagura tsukanda</i>

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:23.000
<i>Koko ni aru "omoi" de sae</i>

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.420
<i>usuragu kioku ni</i>

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:33.640
<i>teikou suru keredo</i>

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:37.140
<i>Kitto koroshi ni kuru</i>

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:43.440
<i>Sugite kita hibi no naka de</i>

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:52.240
<i>tatta hitotsu shinjirareru</i>

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:58.580
<i>Koe o karasete naita</i>

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:01.920
<i>Koko e kite</i>

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.590
<i>Soba ni ite</i>

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:09.220
<i>Nee</i>
